PAGES=[page('076_page_2.jpg',176,[heading('Review Exercise 6'),heading('1. Choose the correct option.')]+[paragraph(num+'. '+q+' '+' '.join('('+l+') '+v for l,v in zip('abcd',opts))) for num,q,opts,a,steps in REVIEW]),page('077_page_1.jpg',177,[heading('Summary'),paragraph('F(x) is an antiderivative of f(x) if F′(x) = f(x).'),paragraph('If F′(x) = f(x), then ∫f(x)dx = F(x)+C, for any real number C. It is called indefinite integral.'),paragraph('If f(x) and g(x) are integral functions w.r.t. x, then the integral of the product of f(x) and g(x) w.r.t. x is:'),eq(r'\int u\,dv=uv-\int v\,du,\quad v=g(x),\quad du=f′(x)\,dx,\quad dv=g′(x)\,dx'),paragraph('If f(x) is continuous on the interval [a,b] and [a,b] is divided into n equal subintervals whose right-hand points are x₁,x₂,...,xₙ, then the definite integral of f(x) from x = a to x = b is:'),eq(r'\int_a^bf(x)\,dx=\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{b-a}n[f(x_1)+f(x_2)+\cdots+f(x_n)],\quad\Delta x=\frac{b-a}n'),eq(r'=\lim_{n\to\infty}\sum_{i=1}^nf(x_i)\Delta x,\quad i=1,2,3,\ldots,n'),paragraph('The definite integral of the product of two functions u and v w.r.t. x is:'),eq(r'\int_a^bu\,dv=[uv]_a^b-\int_a^bv\,du'),paragraph('If f(x) is continuous and f(x) ≥ 0 on the closed interval [a,b], then the area under a curve y = f(x) on [a,b] is given by the definite integral of f(x) on [a,b]:'),eq(r'\mathrm{Area}=\int_a^bf(x)\,dx=F(b)-F(a)'),paragraph('If a function f(x) is continuous on the closed interval [a,b], then'),eq(r'\int_a^bf(x)\,dx=[F(x)]_a^b=F(b)-F(a)'),paragraph('Where F(x) is any function such that F′(x) = f(x) for all x in [a,b].'),note('The source parts wording refers loosely to a product of f,g or u,v; the displayed rule is ∫u dv = ∫u(x)v′(x)dx, not simply ∫u(x)v(x)dx. Choose u = f(x),v = g(x) in its first display. The unsigned area formula needs f ≥ 0; for a sign-changing curve use ∫|f| with sign-change splits. The unit’s opening source pages 142–157 remain unavailable.')])]
